 			<p>Tearing off the blank side of one of her newly copied pages, Jo drew the table before her mother, well knowing that money for the long, sad journey must be borrowed, and feeling as if she could do anything to add a little to the sum for her father.</p>
 			<p>“Now go, dear; but don’t kill yourself driving at a desperate pace; there is no need of that.”</p>
 			<p><abbr epub:type="z3998:name-title">Mrs.</abbr> March’s warning was evidently thrown away; for five minutes later Laurie tore by the window on his own fleet horse, riding as if for his life.</p>
